{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1469844-how-can-social-maneuvering-work-when-someone-can-go-home-to-an-echo-chamber","id":1469844,"title":"How can Social maneuvering work when someone can \"Go home\" to an echo chamber?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-12-07T09:08:49-08:00","id":1469844,"title":"How can Social maneuvering work when someone can \"Go home\" to an echo chamber?","content":"ideas comments something im missing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T10:28:20-08:00","id":1469854,"title":"","content":"My short answer would be that Social Maneuvering attempts (even those to close Doors someone else opened) should be specific to a goal. <br /> For example, if you\u2019re persuading someone to donate to a cause, they might go home and listen to their echo chamber about the economy being in a bad state or that greed is a virtue - but that isn\u2019t providing specific points that contradict /this/ cause. Someone being in that echo chamber would certainly be worth a penalty, but I wouldn\u2019t rule that it automatically closes the Doors you open.<br /> Based on how Social Maneuvering works, I\u2019d also rule that a person can\u2019t use it on themself. That is, if you make progress persuading someone, they won\u2019t go looking for counterarguments - that should probably only occur from a failure or dramatic failure (justifying why that door stays shut, not to shut more Doors).<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2026But if it\u2019s about a prominent social issue, or the data mining is accurate enough, the eco chamber might just be specific enough to be actively closing Doors. And you just can\u2019t change their minds about that subject - until you have a way to get them out of the echo chamber, or switch to a tangential argument that\u2019s not specifically targeted, or make it personal and specific enough to not get shouted down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 12-07-2021, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T11:12:21-08:00","id":1469856,"title":"","content":"Friends, counselors, and advisors would be a similar factor to this, I do believe - unknown sources of opposition to your social maneuvering attempts. It\u2019s very reasonable that a person gets a second opinion from someone close to them, especially while still making a decision about an exciting or nerve-wracking subject. <br /> <br /> One way around this is to choose your mark - find someone who doesn\u2019t have confidants (or an echo chamber) working against you.<br /> Another way is to make your arguments in a way that doesn\u2019t raise opposition. Like, if the target feels like it\u2019s a Small Deal, they might not talk it over with others. This could be an optional benefit for an exceptional success, or using Subterfuge over another skill.<br /> Finally, if the target does have a confidant (or echo chamber) that closes a Door, lampshade that to the players. Have the target be more closed off at the next meeting, and literally say the counterpoints they heard - maybe even the source. Let the players know that there\u2019s significant opposition to what they\u2019re trying to do, and make them deal with that before making progress.<br /> <br /> I find it reasonable, and both true to life and true to the genre, that not everyone is \u2018vulnerable\u2019 to Social Maneuvering; their social networks are too strong to allow any leverage. Success becomes a matter of finding \u201cthe weakest link\u201d, or cutting someone off from their network, or gaining a form of leverage that can\u2019t be so easily contradicted. And even then, it\u2019s dramatically appropriate for them to have a crisis of conscience or sudden back up just after following through with the demands, (in a \u201csuccess with complications\u201d fashion).<br /> <br /> The counterbalance to this is that persuasion can work on many different levels, from many different types of argument. Something that appeals to a person\u2019s Virtue will get to them on a much deeper level than their social network can contradict; fanning their emotions works really well in the short term, but might lose all progress once they have a chance to cool down and think it over.<br /> This is something I think Exalted 3rd Ed did really well, and isn\u2019t well reflected in CoD\u2019s mechanics. Situational modifiers can get into this a bit, but\u2026 <br /> I have Thoughts, many of which are still half-baked, but my \u2018long\u2019 answer is creating a new hack. Or system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 12-07-2021, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T13:41:52-08:00","id":1469867,"title":"","content":"Was thinking about it because The Hunter Darkness and light fan supplement the Stars of bethlahem are misguided philanthropists who would probaly like to convince the sensitives of their POV But the sensitives would like to do same thing to them convince them to &quot;Leave us be Help out if you will but stop acting like your the grown ups in charge&quot; its a lot simpler to win social maneuvering if you improve their disposition towards you to the point things get done in a single encounter&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T13:43:12-08:00","id":1469868,"title":"","content":"It would work by the dramatic convention that your persuasive arguments and leverage are sufficient to overcome other influences by virtue of the effort that you put in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T13:58:44-08:00","id":1469869,"title":"","content":"another thing Won't hide this about myself I'm an inactivist someone said publicly that they felt sorry for me and could tell from my videos on YouTube I had developmental disorders and felt I was being used by the inactivists when I've belonged to this human rights issue my entire adult life and apprenticed a young person into it.<br /> <br /> I felt uncomfortable maybe he was sincere but what if he was hostile to my cause and trying to rob it of a veteran activist?Even if h e was sincere he was a misguided philanthropist at best. I blocked him on facebook without a word He followed me over o nto youtube And I Deleted his post s both of them without a word. with the second and final post on youtube he seemed desperate to get me to speak to him. <br /> <br /> Is that social maneuvering that kind of deliberate targeted refusal to engage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-07T15:15:42-08:00","id":1469876,"title":"","content":"If I were to describe that situation and outcome through a social maneuvering attempt, it would probably be that person trying to engage social maneuvering with you, failing the roll, and developing a worse impression - it sounds like to \u201chostile\u201d, where no further actions can be attempted.<br /> <br /> Refusing to engage with someone would not be an action it itself (it would be having a hostile impression toward them); convincing someone to leave you alone would probably be a social maneuvering action, though.<br /> <br /> And yeah, boosting your impression to open all doors in one encounter is definitely one strategy to overcome outside influences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T07:31:50-08:00","id":1469916,"title":"","content":"One thing is if you succeed in a social maneuvering roll and they go back home to an echo chamber that finds out what he did.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T10:44:58-08:00","id":1469932,"title":"","content":"Just use the normal rules, apply a penalty or more Doors to represent the Echo Chamber.<br /> <br /> The Echo Chamber is a strong effect, but not insurmountable, It isn't simple to overcome, true, but that's why you throw dice using your character's skills instead of coming with the solution yourself.<br /> <br /> Social Maneuvering is already the system to deal with complex interactions, where someone is unlikely to be convinced of something, but you can work over time to change that.<br /> <br /> Convince a person of something contrary to their Echo Chamber is basically a textbook case of Social Maneuvering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-09T23:33:02-08:00","id":1470113,"title":"","content":"ideas what happens if they succumb then go home to an echo chamber?<br /> <br /> &quot;Waiit did I really do that Guess I did&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-10T14:56:42-08:00","id":1470168,"title":"","content":"There's a difference between an echo chamber and a cult... echo chambers enforce some level of social norms, but at the same time primarily exist to justify a permission structure. A &quot;normal&quot; echo chamber isn't some super intrusive group of people that analyze everything you do, expecting constant updates on daily decisions, and so on. If a character is convinced to do something that would be seen as embarrassing/shameful to the echo chamber, they're either not going to say anything, or couch it in terms to seek validations for their lapse in judgement and avoid negative responses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-10T23:09:11-07:00","id":1480729,"title":"","content":"oh on social maneuvering<br /> <br /> <br /> was wondering what distinction is between intimidation and forcing doors<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> one real life example, A few years back me and my dad were helpin to transplant my stuff from my old apartment to my new one and I was alone for a bit and a pair of evangedlists accosted me saying &quot;Want to get bapitzed right now?&quot;<br /> <br /> I was about to start screaming &quot;Religous harassment!!!&quot; At top of my lungs but my dad came in and saw us and called out a threat to report them to the office","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T00:48:24-07:00","id":1480731,"title":"","content":"The difference is whether the ST feels a normal roll off is better, or taking account Doors for Forcing them is better (esp. if Hard Leverage is going to be involved).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T02:53:44-07:00","id":1480735,"title":"","content":"Honestly I can very much see intimidation being part of a normal social maneuvering attempt. I'm imagining something like a group of criminals setting up a protection racket, but I'm sure others can think of other situations where it makes sense. Intimidation is just a way to (attempt to) get people to do what you want.<br /> <br /> Forcing doors is just an attempt to get it done right now, and can be done any way you want. Guilt tripping is probably another easy way to imagine. It's the sledgehammer to social maneuvering's scapel.<br /> <br /> Then there's the situations where you're not even considering doing it over the long term, for which you'd likely just do a contested or resisted roll. Getting a bunch of thugs to back down so you can get away with the McGuffin, or convincing the bouncer to let you into the VIP area. Just situations where if you visit them again tomorrow you're not going to be dealing with this. I'd argue your evangelist encounter was actually this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-11T17:44:19-07:00","id":1480786,"title":"","content":"A detail to bear in mind about Forcing Doors is how it &quot;burn the door&quot; for you. It's not just the &quot;I want it now&quot; route, but the <i>All or Nothing</i> nature of it. Observe that the text explicitly says that at failing the target becomes immune to Social Maneuvering from you. No time or condition, they're immune <b>forever</b>.<br /> <br /> You encounter is certainly a great example. Convincing you to baptize and begin in their church wasn't something a simple attempt was likely to succeed at, so they tried a desperate tactic. Now I doubt you'll even consider listening to anything they say if you ever recognize them again in any other context, or at least you'll be very wary of them.<br /> <br /> This is beyond simple Intimidation and Intimidation can be used in Social Maneuvering without such effect. In the US this is standard procedure for police interrogations, it is basically Social Maneuvering using Intimidation, among other things, but still working in the long run instead of rushing things up too much, even if they set up the situation to maximize time and success (there are cases of interrogations taking 18 hours).<br /> <br /> Every time the character going for a Social Maneuvering decides it's time for a <i>Now or Never</i> tactic, this is Forcing Doors and failure means <i>Never</i>.<br /> <br /> By the way, that's another thing to be said about the rule on Social Maneuvering. It doesn't have to be a positive interaction, as the target doesn't have to be convinced due to liking you. It can be a cult brainwashing, it can convince you little by little that you'l get in trouble if you don't do this or that, it can be anything.<br /> <br /> I even argued in the past that Social Maneuvering is the best rule to model torture, because it is basically what torture does: it uses pain and abuse, physical and psychological, to convince you to do something. Some people say that torture doesn't work, but that isn't true. Torture doesn't work <b>for getting the truth</b>, which Social Maneuvering doesn't do either, it works to convince you to <b>do</b> something, even if this something is to confess (regardless of your confession being true or not).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-17T03:06:16-07:00","id":1481281,"title":"","content":"Personally, I tend to go with 'it can work because the rules says it works.' The system itself is an abstraction of how you persuade someone to do something they weren't inclined to do in the first place, that's the label on the tin, and that's how I let it work in my games.<br /> <br /> I don't really feel like adding a bunch of whataboutit's to the mechanics of these game (i.e I've seen a lot of peopel go 'well actually that's not how this gun would work' etc), so just go with the flow of the story and don't overcomplicate things.","s